WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.101
When I was young,

00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:16.458
I wanted to be on TV:

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.309
the lights, the cameras,

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:21.976
the makeup,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.417
the glamorous life.

00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:26.101
And from my vantage point,

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:29.726
just outside of a military base
in Lawton, Oklahoma,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.726
I didn't make the distinction
between TV reporter or actor.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.351
It was all the same to me.

00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:36.643
It was either,

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.059
"Reporting live from Berlin"

00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:42.518
or "I shall attend her here and woo her
with such spirit when she comes."

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.809
(Laughter)

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:45.434
It was all special,

00:00:45.458 --> 00:00:47.184
it was all the spotlight,

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:49.833
and I just knew that it was for me.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:52.833
But somewhere along my journey,

00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:55.875
life happened.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.143
Ah, much better.

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:36.101
(Applause)

00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:37.875
I have a disease called vitiligo.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.708
It started early in my career.

00:02:42.542 --> 00:02:44.792
It's an autoimmune disorder.

00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:49.184
It's where it looks like your skin
is getting white patches,

00:02:49.208 --> 00:02:50.875
but it's actually void of color.

00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:54.018
It affects all ethnicities,

00:02:54.042 --> 00:02:55.750
it affects all ages,

00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:58.226
all genders,

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.643
it's not contagious,

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.851
it's not life-threatening,

00:03:01.875 --> 00:03:04.417
but it is mental warfare.

00:03:05.458 --> 00:03:06.708
It's tough.

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:09.268
Now, I was diagnosed with this disease

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:12.125
when I was working on
"Eyewitness News" in New York City.

00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:15.934
I was in the biggest city in the country,

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:17.875
I was on their flagship station

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.018
and I was on their top-rated 5pm newscast.

00:03:23.042 --> 00:03:25.643
And the doctor looked me
right in the eye and said,

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.434
"You have a disease called vitiligo.

00:03:27.458 --> 00:03:30.917
It's a skin disorder
where you lose your pigment.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.851
There is no cure,
but there a-la-la-la-la".

00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:36.393
Charlie Brown's teacher.

00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:37.434
(Laughter)

00:03:37.458 --> 00:03:42.583
He said there is no cure.
All I heard was, "My career is over."

00:03:44.042 --> 00:03:45.583
But I just couldn't give up.

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.375
I couldn't quit,

00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:53.184
because we put too much into this.

00:03:53.208 --> 00:03:55.476
And by "we" I mean Mr. Moss,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.851
who sent me to speech and drama club
instead of to detention,

00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:03.934
or my sister who paid
part of my college expenses,

00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:05.208
or my mom,

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:11.042
who simply gave me everything.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:16.917
I would not quit.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:23.125
So I decided to just put on makeup
and keep it moving.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.976
I had to wear makeup anyway.
It's TV, baby, right?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.041
I just put on a little more makeup,
and everything's cool.

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:36.476
And that actually
went very well for years.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.018
I went from being a reporter
in New York City

00:04:40.042 --> 00:04:42.726
to being a morning show anchor in Detroit,

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.643
the Motor City.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.559
And as the disease got worse,

00:04:47.583 --> 00:04:49.643
I just put on more makeup.

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.518
It was easy.

00:04:51.542 --> 00:04:54.250
Except for my hands.

00:04:55.458 --> 00:04:58.809
See, this disease is progressive
and ever-changing.

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:01.309
That means it comes and goes.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.476
At one point, for about a year and a half,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.250
my face was completely white.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.768
Yeah, it trips me out too.

00:05:11.792 --> 00:05:13.101
(Laughter)

00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:14.375
Yeah.

00:05:14.958 --> 00:05:18.768
And then, with a little help,

00:05:18.792 --> 00:05:21.768
some of the pigment came back,

00:05:21.792 --> 00:05:24.559
but living through this process

00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:26.292
was like two sides of a coin.

00:05:28.125 --> 00:05:30.184
When I'm at work
and I'm wearing the makeup

00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:32.518
or wearing the makeup outside,
I'm the TV guy.

00:05:32.542 --> 00:05:34.726
"Hey, how you doing everybody? Great."

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.226
At home without the makeup,

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.625
I'd take it off
and it was like being a leper.

00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:44.018
The stares, constantly staring at me,

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:47.393
the comments under their breath.

00:05:47.417 --> 00:05:49.434
Some people refused to shake my hand.

00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:52.184
Some people moved
to the other side of the sidewalk,

00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:54.143
moved to the other side of the elevator.

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:56.958
I felt like they were moving
to the other side of life.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.518
It was tough,

00:06:01.542 --> 00:06:04.042
and those were some tough years.

00:06:06.417 --> 00:06:07.809
And honestly,

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.851
sometimes I just had to shelter in place.

00:06:10.875 --> 00:06:12.184
You know what I mean?

00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:15.125
Kind of just stay at home
till I get my mind right.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.292
But then I'd put my blinders back on,

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.625
I'd get back out there,

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.434
do my thing,

00:06:24.458 --> 00:06:26.393
but in the process of doing that,

00:06:26.417 --> 00:06:28.167
I developed this --

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.708
angry, grumpy demeanor.

00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:35.601
Anger is an easy go-to,

00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:37.851
and people would leave me alone,

00:06:37.875 --> 00:06:40.125
but it just wasn't me.

00:06:41.417 --> 00:06:42.976
It wasn't me.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.458
I was allowing this disease to turn me
into this angry, grumpy, spotted guy.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.542
It just wasn't me.

00:06:51.583 --> 00:06:53.000
So I had to change.

00:06:54.583 --> 00:06:57.750
I knew I could not change other people.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.458
People are going to react
and do what they gonna do.

00:07:02.708 --> 00:07:04.958
But there was a cold hard reality as well.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.101
I was the one

00:07:10.125 --> 00:07:14.143
that was showing anger, sadness

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.101
and isolating myself.

00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:17.417
It was actually a choice.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.559
I was walking out the door every day

00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:25.976
expecting the world
to react with negativity,

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.708
so I just gave them that mean face first.

00:07:30.958 --> 00:07:35.625
If I wanted change,
the change had to start with me.

00:07:37.417 --> 00:07:39.542
So I came up with a plan.

00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:43.708
Two-parter, not that deep.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.518
Number one: I would just let people stare,

00:07:48.542 --> 00:07:51.268
drink it in, stare all you want,

00:07:51.292 --> 00:07:53.351
and not react.

00:07:53.375 --> 00:07:56.018
Because the truth is
when I got this disease,

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:59.601
I was all up in the mirror
staring at every new spot

00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:02.268
trying to figure out what is going on.

00:08:02.292 --> 00:08:05.833
So I needed to let other people
have that same opportunity

00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:09.458
to get that visual understanding.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:12.500
Number two:

00:08:14.625 --> 00:08:16.500
I would react with positivity,

00:08:18.125 --> 00:08:20.226
and that was simply a smile,

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.393
or, at the very least,

00:08:22.417 --> 00:08:25.625
a nonjudgmental, kind face.

00:08:26.875 --> 00:08:28.125
Simple plan.

00:08:29.042 --> 00:08:31.583
But it turned out to be
more difficult than I thought.

00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:34.583
But over time,

00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:36.958
things started to go OK.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.143
Like this one time, I'm at the store
and this dude is like staring at me,

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:45.226
like burning a hole
in the side of my head.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.851
I'm shopping, he's staring at me,

00:08:46.875 --> 00:08:49.058
I'm going to the checkout,
he's staring at me,

00:08:49.082 --> 00:08:52.601
I'm checking out, he's on the other line
checking out, he's staring at me,

00:08:52.625 --> 00:08:54.726
we go to the exit,
he's still staring at me,

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:56.851
so I see he's staring

00:08:56.875 --> 00:08:59.726
and finally I turn to him
and I go, "Hey buddy, what's up!"

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.018
And he goes ...

00:09:01.042 --> 00:09:02.643
(Mumbles nervously) "Hi!"

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:03.684
(Laughter)

00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:05.976
Awkward.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.518
So to relieve the tension, I say,

00:09:08.542 --> 00:09:10.309
"It's just a skin disorder.

00:09:10.333 --> 00:09:12.559
It's not contagious,
it's not life-threatening,

00:09:12.583 --> 00:09:14.643
it just makes me look a little different."

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:17.309
I end up talking to that guy
for like five minutes.

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:19.726
It was kind of cool, right?

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.833
And at the end
of our conversation, he says,

00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:26.726
"You know, if you
didn't have 'vitilargo'" --

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.809
it's actually vitiligo,
but he was trying, so --

00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:31.309
(Laughter)

00:09:31.333 --> 00:09:35.018
"if you didn't have vitilargo,
you'd look just like that guy on TV."

00:09:35.042 --> 00:09:36.309
(Laughter)

00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:40.434
And I was like, "Haha,
yeah, I get that, I get that, yeah."

00:09:40.458 --> 00:09:41.934
(Laughter)

00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:43.875
So things were going OK.

00:09:45.208 --> 00:09:48.125
I was having more good exchanges than bad,

00:09:49.542 --> 00:09:52.792
until that day.

00:09:54.792 --> 00:09:56.309
I had a little time before work

00:09:56.333 --> 00:09:58.851
so I like to stop by the park
to watch the kids play.

00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:00.143
They're funny.

00:10:00.167 --> 00:10:03.476
So I got a little too close,
this little girl wasn't paying attention,

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.226
she's about two or three years old,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.684
she's running, she runs directly
into my leg and falls down, pretty hard.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.059
I thought she hurt herself,

00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:12.476
so I reach out to try
and help the little girl

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.143
and she looks at my vitiligo

00:10:14.167 --> 00:10:17.667
and she screams!

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.143
Now kids are pure honesty.

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.101
She's like two or three.

00:10:30.125 --> 00:10:34.184
This little girl,
she wasn't trying to be mean.

00:10:34.208 --> 00:10:36.684
She didn't have any malice in her heart.

00:10:36.708 --> 00:10:38.417
This little girl was afraid.

00:10:39.875 --> 00:10:41.125
She was just afraid.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.059
I didn't know what to do.

00:10:46.083 --> 00:10:48.542
I just took a step back
and put my hands by my side.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:57.208
I stayed in the house for two weeks
and three days on that one.

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:02.684
It took me a second
to get my mind around the fact

00:11:02.708 --> 00:11:04.750
that I scare small children.

00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:09.875
And that was something
that I could not smile away.

00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:16.833
But I jumped back on my plan

00:11:19.875 --> 00:11:22.542
and just put on my blinders,

00:11:23.542 --> 00:11:24.833
started going back out.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:29.559
Two months later, I'm in a grocery store
reaching on the bottom shelf,

00:11:29.583 --> 00:11:32.333
and I hear a little voice go,
"You've got a boo-boo?"

00:11:33.583 --> 00:11:37.268
It's like a two-year-old, three-year-old,
same age, little girl,

00:11:37.292 --> 00:11:38.708
but she's not crying,

00:11:39.875 --> 00:11:42.768
so I kneel down in front of her

00:11:42.792 --> 00:11:45.393
and I don't speak two-year-old
so I look up at the mom,

00:11:45.417 --> 00:11:46.893
and I say, "What did she say?"

00:11:46.917 --> 00:11:49.601
And she says, "She thinks
you have a boo-boo."

00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:53.059
So I go, "No, I don't have
a boo-boo, no, not at all."

00:11:53.083 --> 00:11:54.851
And the little girl says,

00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:56.167
"Duh-duh-hoy?"

00:11:57.167 --> 00:11:59.601
And so I look to mom for the translation,

00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:00.976
and she says,

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.292
"She thinks you're hurt."

00:12:03.542 --> 00:12:08.059
And I say, "No, sweetie,
I'm not hurt at all, I'm fine."

00:12:08.083 --> 00:12:11.351
And the little girl
reaches out with that little hand

00:12:11.375 --> 00:12:13.684
and touches my face.

00:12:13.708 --> 00:12:16.101
She's trying to rub
the chocolate into the vanilla

00:12:16.125 --> 00:12:17.434
or whatever she was doing.

00:12:17.458 --> 00:12:18.708
It was amazing!

00:12:19.667 --> 00:12:20.917
It was awesome.

00:12:21.875 --> 00:12:23.934
Because she thought she knew what it was,

00:12:23.958 --> 00:12:25.934
she was giving me everything I wanted:

00:12:25.958 --> 00:12:28.684
kindness, compassion.

00:12:28.708 --> 00:12:30.625
And with the touch of that little hand,

00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:35.226
she healed a grown man's pain.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.809
Yee-ha.

00:12:37.833 --> 00:12:39.083
Healed.

00:12:42.333 --> 00:12:44.625
I smiled for a long time on that one.

00:12:47.708 --> 00:12:51.875
Positivity is something
worth fighting for,

00:12:52.958 --> 00:12:55.934
and the fight is not with others --

00:12:55.958 --> 00:12:57.208
it's internal.

00:12:58.458 --> 00:13:02.125
If you want to make
positive changes in your life,

00:13:03.625 --> 00:13:08.417
you have to consistently be positive.

00:13:13.167 --> 00:13:15.476
My blood type is actually B positive.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.851
(Laughter)

00:13:18.875 --> 00:13:21.268
I know, corny TV guy dad joke,

00:13:21.292 --> 00:13:23.268
my daughter hates it, but I don't care!

00:13:23.292 --> 00:13:25.018
Be positive!

00:13:25.042 --> 00:13:27.500
(Laughs)

00:13:32.583 --> 00:13:35.226
A 14-year-old boy years ago --

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.309
this kid had vitiligo --

00:13:37.333 --> 00:13:41.268
he asked me to show my face on television.

00:13:41.292 --> 00:13:42.726
I wasn't going to do it,

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.559
we've been over this,
I thought I was going to lose my job,

00:13:45.583 --> 00:13:47.792
but the kid convinced me by saying,

00:13:48.875 --> 00:13:53.226
"If you show people what you look like
and explain this to them,

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.417
maybe they will treat me differently."

00:13:56.458 --> 00:13:59.042
Boom! Blinders off.

00:13:59.833 --> 00:14:02.184
I did a TV report,

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:04.250
got an overwhelming response.

00:14:05.375 --> 00:14:06.934
So I didn't know what to do.

00:14:06.958 --> 00:14:09.684
I took the attention
and focused it back on the kid

00:14:09.708 --> 00:14:11.458
and other people that have vitiligo.

00:14:12.417 --> 00:14:13.958
I started a support group.

00:14:15.125 --> 00:14:18.059
Pretty soon, we noticed "VITFriends"

00:14:18.083 --> 00:14:22.792
and "V-Strong" support groups
all over the country.

00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:30.208
In 2016, we all came together
and celebrated World Vitiligo Day.

00:14:32.833 --> 00:14:35.059
This past June 25,

00:14:35.083 --> 00:14:37.976
we had over 300 people,

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.893
all in celebration of our annual event.

00:14:42.917 --> 00:14:44.167
It was amazing.

00:14:44.792 --> 00:14:46.351
(Applause)

00:14:46.375 --> 00:14:47.625
Thanks.

00:14:52.208 --> 00:14:54.768
Now, I'm not going to lie to you

00:14:54.792 --> 00:14:57.768
and say it was quick or easy

00:14:57.792 --> 00:15:02.083
for me to find a positive place
living with this disease,

00:15:03.417 --> 00:15:04.667
but I found it.

00:15:06.708 --> 00:15:08.417
But I also got much more.

00:15:10.083 --> 00:15:13.018
I became a better man,

00:15:13.042 --> 00:15:15.309
the man I always wanted to be,

00:15:15.333 --> 00:15:21.018
the kind of guy who can stand up
in front of a room full of strangers

00:15:21.042 --> 00:15:24.292
and tell some of
the toughest stories in his life

00:15:25.625 --> 00:15:27.250
and end it all with a smile,

00:15:29.458 --> 00:15:34.208
and find happiness in the fact
that you all just smiled back.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:36.518
Thank you.

00:15:36.542 --> 00:15:39.083
(Applause)

